  "id": "COMPOUND:21234 - PROTEIN:377",
  "verbalization": "Stilbostemin B 3'-Beta-D-Glucopyranoside is implicated in the pathway leading to Riboflavin synthase through multiple indirect routes. The drug acts as a target for Cyanovirin-N, which in turn is targeted by other compounds, including [(1R)-1-[(5R)-4-Bromo-5-(Iodomethyl)-5-Methoxy-2-Oxofuran-3-Yl]Butyl] Acetate and Methyl 2-acetyl-3,5-dihydroxyphenylacetate. These latter molecules all ultimately target Riboflavin synthase, suggesting a shared mechanism of action involving the enzyme. The evidence points to a potential regulatory or inhibitory relationship between Stilbostemin B 3'-Beta-D-Glucopyranoside and Riboflavin synthase, possibly through the modulation of downstream targets. The integration of these pathways highlights a possible role for Stilbostemin B 3'-Beta-D-Glucopyranoside in influencing the activity of Riboflavin synthase via its interaction with Cyanovirin-N and other compounds that ultimately affect the enzyme.",
